Neko Project 21/W
-----------------

Derived material, and where it came from upstream:

  core/bios/crt.c        the CRT parameter table (`crtdata`), the cursor
                         form table (`csrform`), the master and slave GDC
                         SYNC parameter sets, and the index arithmetic of
                         the INT 18h AH=30h display-mode service.
                         From np21w bios/bios18.c.

  core/lib/hwinit.c      the power-on I/O write table for the DMA
                         controller, PIT and interrupt controllers
                         (`hw_table`).  From np21w bios/bios.c.
                         The two interrupt-mask seed values at the end of
                         that table are NOT from np21w; they were measured
                         on a real PC-9821Xa7.

  include/pc98/gdc.h     the uPD7220 command opcodes and the mode
                         flip-flop bit numbers.  From np21w io/gdc_cmd.h
                         and io/gdc.c.  (These are hardware constants and
                         are listed here out of caution rather than
                         because the selection is obviously expressive.)

Two further files name np21w in their comments but carry no code from it,
and are listed only so the citation is not mistaken for a derivation:

  core/bios/disk.c       cites np21w's SXSI disk BIOS for the INT 1Bh
                         CALL CONVENTION, which is a PC-98 interface, not
                         an implementation.  The implementation here is
                         unrelated.

  include/pc98/wa.h      cites np21w for the NAMES of published work-area
                         fields.  The addresses were measured.

